                <pb facs="0529" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/5–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-05-13T12:00:00+09:00">May 13, 1948—noon.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 13—4:29 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>868. For Department and ECA. Embassy agrees entirely with statement general
                    policy contained Deptel 696, May 7 and will forward shortly its specific
                    recommendations re number and strategic location for advisors to Chinese
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Shanghai 379.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
